# oracle: fix srd with a fix deform that scales the box (x and y scale 1.25, constant rate), no thermostat: the SRD streaming velocity h_rate and the bins that follow the box, 2d (cut-down of examples/ASPHERE/line/in.line.srd: the deform phase on point SRD particles, 3x3 box, 200 steps)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-13 abs=1e-14
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): the engine agrees with every thermo column to a relative error of 1e-13 (also at abs 1e-14) and with the positions and velocities of every atom to an absolute error of 1e-14 (the largest is 1.0e-14, a velocity of about 16). The SRD thermostat with the same deformation (tstat yes) is tests/oracle/w256srd_deform_tstat (its per-atom state is chaotic: round-off at step 0 grows about 1.3x per step, as a native self-perturbation shows, so that case runs 150 steps); unbiased yes is w79srd_deform_unbias.
units		lj
atom_style	atomic
atom_modify	first empty
dimension	2

lattice		sq 0.4
region		box block 0 3 0 3 -0.5 0.5
create_box	1 box

lattice		sq 0.4
region		plane block 0 3 0 3 -0.001 0.001
lattice		sq 85.0
create_atoms	1 region plane

group		empty type 2

mass		1 0.01
velocity	all create 1.0 593849 loop geom

neighbor	0.3 bin
neigh_modify	delay 1 every 1 check no

comm_modify	group empty

timestep	0.02

fix		1 all srd 1 NULL 1.0 0.25 49894 collision slip
fix		2 all enforce2d
fix		3 all deform 1 x scale 1.25 y scale 1.25

thermo_style	custom step temp f_1[7] etotal press f_1[3] f_1[4] f_1[6]
thermo_modify	format float %.15g
thermo		20

run		200
